DESCRIPTION:Scholars and critics alike have observed a return to realism i
 n award-winning 21st-century American fiction\, particularly in works by a
 uthors such as Jonathan Franzen\, Jonathan Safran Foer\, Eric Puchner\, an
 d Zadie Smith. This return is reflected both in formal features\, includin
 g third-person heterodiegetic narration and mimetic representation\, and i
 n recurring thematic concerns such as the family saga\, the middle class\,
  and domestic life.\n\nIn this talk\, Leniarska will discuss some of the r
 esult\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://cesta.stanford.edu\nLast synced: 
 2026-09-24 10:45 PDT
LOCATION:Building 160\, Wallenberg Hall
URL:https://cesta.stanford.edu
END:VEVENT
