BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[The Ho Center for Buddhist Studies] Jane Casey: “Establishing C
 hronology in Tibetan Art: A Study of Taklung Paintings”
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260924T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260924T183000
DTSTAMP:20260924T174557Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53862496557289-53862496558314@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Abstract:\n\nThis lecture addresses chronology in early Tibeta
 n art. Dr. Casey highlights over a decade of research on a group of approx
 imately 100 paintings from Taklung and Riwoche monasteries in Tibet. The m
 ain purpose of the study has been to establish a reliable foundation for a
 ssigning dates to Taklung paintings. The Taklung painting corpus particula
 rly lends itself to the task of building a chronology. Almost three quarte
 rs of the paintings bear inscriptions with chronological implications.\n\n
 Ages: All ages\nSource: https://buddhiststudies.stanford.edu/events/jane-c
 asey-establishing-chronology-tibetan-art-study-taklung-paintings\nLast syn
 ced: 2026-09-24 10:45 PDT
LOCATION:Lathrop Library
URL:https://buddhiststudies.stanford.edu/events/jane-casey-establishing-ch
 ronology-tibetan-art-study-taklung-paintings
END:VEVENT
